From d105cc75534a8dcdd1957844c761e7f214a7ecbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:54:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] DocumentsUI: use static paper-and-ink presentation

Drawer completion and list dividers (folded from 0002-drawer-completion-and-list-dividers): DocumentsDrawerLayout completes open, close and release settles immediately (drawer, nav rail and breadcrumb paths), and directory and root lists draw visible black separators (EinkListDividers).

Material 3 is on (Lineage's static DocumentsUIOverlay sets force_material3, and every legacy layout, style and drawable id is mapped to its M3 twin), so the legacy-only overrides are gone: 17 res-eink colours, 14 res-eink drawables (incl. the unused gradient_actionbar_background), the legacy res-eink styles, text styles and dimens, the v31/night-v31/sw720dp values, the unreachable colour entries, and the edits to the legacy drawer_layout and item_doc_header_message layouts.

On-colours on black (primary, secondary, tertiary, error, success) are white, so the grid check mark and the drag copy badge show; list rules skip selected or focused rows and their neighbours; the current breadcrumb is plain, not dashed (disabled); checked filter chips are inverted; the snackbar tint keeps its edge (multiply); the sort sheet strokes the shape drawable BottomSheetBehavior installs.

Dialogs are plain MaterialAlertDialogBuilder dialogs and the popup menu background a plain 4dp shape, so the floating-window border (FlatWindowBorder) draws their only edge from the native outline (EinkAlertDialogBuilder and EinkShapeDrawable, which hid that outline behind a 1px stroke, are gone). In-window edges are whole-pixel 1dp (2px at 300dpi); selected, activated and checked rows, cards and rail items use a 2dp edge, the selected tab indicator is 2dp, dashes are 3dp/2dp; the drawer edge stays a 1px line. The search bar keeps one edge around its pill (no box around the bar).
